#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SessionStart hook: inject a short Drupal project brief plus the skill routing table, only when the
# cwd is inside a Drupal project. Output: {"hookSpecificOutput":{...,"additionalContext":"..."}} or nothing.
set -u
PLUGIN="${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/../.." && pwd)}"
. "$PLUGIN/scripts/lib/common.sh"

input=$(cat 2>/dev/null || true)
cwd=$(printf '%s' "$input" | sed -n 's/.*"cwd":"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' | head -1)
[ -z "$cwd" ] && cwd=$(pwd)

read -r KIND ROOT <<<"$(dsp_find_root "$cwd")"
[ "$KIND" = "none" ] && exit 0

profile=$("$PLUGIN/scripts/drupal-profile" "$cwd" --summary 2>/dev/null | head -6)
runtime=$("$PLUGIN/scripts/drupal-runtime" "$cwd" --quick --summary 2>/dev/null | head -3)
[ -z "$profile" ] && exit 0

ctx="Drupal project detected (drupal-superpowers).
$profile
$runtime
Facts above come from files, not memory; anything not listed is unknown until checked.
Language rule: write ALL code, machine names, identifiers, comments, docblocks, YAML labels, tests, and reports in English, whatever language the user writes in; user-facing strings are English inside t()/TranslatableMarkup so Drupal translates them.

Two rules in this repo: (1) invoke the matching drupal-superpowers skill BEFORE the first investigation or edit; (2) never end a reply that says done, fixed, works, or passes without invoking drupal-verification first, even for a one-line change. When Superpowers is installed, its process skills (brainstorming, systematic-debugging, writing-plans) run first and these run inside them.

Skill routing (several can apply in sequence):
- version, paths, runtime, or commands unknown → drupal-project-understanding
- build / change / fix something in this Drupal project (no Superpowers process skill active) → drupal-workflow
- unsure an API, service, hook, or method exists, or asked to use a named one → drupal-research
- architectural-class design (new entity/config type, integration, permission model, cross-module behaviour) or a design/brainstorming discussion → drupal-architecture (escalates the turn to the strongest model; bounded changes read its decision tables instead)
- creating/editing module files: .info/.services/.routing/.permissions.yml, controllers, forms, plugins, entities, hooks → drupal-module-development
- choosing or writing PHPUnit/Kernel/Functional tests, or a Drupal test fails → drupal-testing
- an error, WSOD, ServiceNotFound, plugin/route not found, or wrong behaviour to diagnose → drupal-debugging
- code touching access, permissions, routes, user data, output/Markup/Twig, queries, uploads, redirects → drupal-security
- render output that varies by user, permissions, language, or query; stale or another user's data → drupal-cacheability
- config/install, schema, sync, drift, cex/cim, config vs state → drupal-config
- any new feature or module, before writing custom code (does core or a contrib module already do it?), or picking a dependency → drupal-contrib-research
- about to run drush/composer/phpunit/phpcs/phpstan, verify on a site, or use Drupal MCP tools → drupal-runtime-verification
- reviewing a diff, module, or PR → drupal-code-review
- about to say done, fixed, working, or passing → drupal-verification
- core/PHP/Symfony upgrades, deprecations, Rector, contrib major bumps → drupal-upgrade
- theme work: Twig templates, libraries.yml, Drupal.behaviors/once, preprocess, SDC components, CSS/JS, markup accessibility → drupal-frontend
- slow page/route/Views/cron/queue, entity loads in loops, per-row queries, profiling, cache hit rate → drupal-performance
- migration YAML, source/process/destination plugins, drush migrate:*, importing from Drupal 7/CSV/JSON/another DB → drupal-migrate-api
- debugging or architecture still unresolved after two falsified hypotheses, intermittent/env-dependent bugs, expensive-to-reverse decisions → drupal-hard-problem (escalates this turn to the strongest model)"

printf '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"SessionStart","additionalContext":%s}}\n' "$(dsp_json quote "$ctx")"
